.el .ds Aq '
.TH sway-things-set 1 "" "Sway Things 0.0.0" "Sway Things Manual"
.SH NAME
sway\-things\-set \- Change a setting: live, in the settings files and in the generated sway config
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsway\-things set\fR [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-\-host\fR] [\fB\-\-shared\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-overwrite\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIKEY\fR> <\fIVALUE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change a setting: live, in the settings files and in the generated sway config
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<IDENTIFIER>\fR
The input device, by its identifier as `swaymsg \-t get_inputs` shows it
.TP
\fB\-\-host\fR
Store the value for this machine only, in settings.d/<hostname>.toml
.TP
\fB\-\-shared\fR
Store the value in the shared settings.toml
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Change a setting that can lock you out without asking to keep it
.TP
\fB\-\-overwrite\fR
Replace generated files that were changed outside Sway Things
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Controls when to use color
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
The setting, e.g. windows.gaps.inner
.TP
<\fIVALUE\fR>
The new value: true or false, a number, a choice, a color as #rrggbb, text, or a list as items separated by commas (us,de)
